  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "This behaviour is inconsistent with the Main Menu, which takes precedent of the cursor over personal mirrors that are closer to the player than it.\n\nSome simple repro steps:\n\n- Enable immersive mode in personal mirror settings (so that it uses a pointer rather than grab highlight).\n\n- Open the personal mirror.\n\n- Bring the personal mirror close enough to you that it's in front of where your Main Menu would appear.\n\n- Open the Main Menu.\n\n- Attempt to navigate.\n\n- Notice that the user is able to interact with the Main Menu just fine despite the personal mirror technically being \"in front\" in physical space.\n\n- Open the chatbox keyboard.\n\n- Attempt to navigate.\n\n- Notice that the user is unable to naturally interact with the chatbox keyboard, because the pointer is hitting the personal mirror before reaching the keyboard.\n\nThis is frustrating because I will sometimes assume that doing this is okay because it's fine for the Main Menu, only to remember it isn't specifically for the chatbox. So I have to close the chatbox, close my mirror, then begin typing again to be able to properly use the keyboard.\n\nI don't have time to collect media for this but wanted to report it regardless.",
